      'A two-minute Short is not a thirty-second script with longer pauses. It needs enough explanation to justify the extra time. Start with one question and one answer, then choose a runtime that lets a viewer follow the connection. In Vidora, the selected duration guides writing; the generated audio still has to prove that the script fits.',
      '## Choose the runtime before generating',
      'Vidora supports dedicated Short targets from 30 to 180 seconds. A per-run selection takes precedence over the channel default; without either, the target is 120 seconds. Check that selection before generating a draft. Changing the intended length after reviewing a script is an editorial decision, not a way to relabel an already-rendered video.',
