      'Vidora can generate chapter information from production segments when that option is enabled. Review it after the final render. Dedicated Short script timestamps are planning guides, not measurements of delivered speech, so they should not be copied directly into a description as if the narration had already been timed.',
      'A reliable check opens the final file and visits each proposed boundary. Confirm that the section starts there, that the previous chapter ends coherently and that the label matches what a viewer hears. Repeat the check after changing the voice, inserting material or editing an earlier section.',
      '## Write labels people can navigate',
      'Use concise labels that name the section, such as the question being answered or the step being performed. Avoid repeating the complete video title for every entry. A label should make sense when scanned by itself, without requiring the viewer to read a promotional sentence first.',
      'Do not force a keyword variant into every chapter. The purpose is navigation. If several sections have nearly identical labels, ask whether the structure is actually clear or whether those sections should be combined. Descriptive wording is more useful than a list of slightly different search phrases.',
      '## Interpret an analyzer warning correctly',
      'Vidora checks for chapters on videos of at least three minutes as a practical metadata heuristic. That threshold is not a universal YouTube rule, and a warning is not evidence of a ranking penalty. Decide whether chapters help this video, then verify the platform requirements and the actual boundaries.',
      '## Check the published result',
